# Packages for TEST images only. Never part of a release.
#
# This file lives under tests/ on purpose: live-build reads every
# config/package-lists/*.list.chroot it finds, so keeping it out of that
# directory is what makes exclusion the default rather than something to
# remember. scripts/build.sh copies it in only when STRATA_TEST_TOOLS=1, and
# removes the copy unconditionally at the start of every build — so an
# interrupted test build cannot leave it behind for a release build to inherit.
#
# qemu-guest-agent lets the host run commands inside the guest over a
# virtio-serial channel and read their real output, instead of typing into the
# VM through simulated keystrokes and reading results off screenshots. That
# difference is not cosmetic: the installed system tracking Debian stable
# instead of testing went unnoticed by every automated check and was found by a
# human running `cat /etc/apt/sources.list` by hand. With guest-exec, that is a
# test.
#
# It is preferred over openssh-server because it opens no network port, needs no
# key management, and does nothing at all without the virtio channel QEMU
# provides — so even if it did escape into an image, it would not be reachable.
qemu-guest-agent
